{#-
  automap-sync (JMWE for Jira Cloud) - push this site's automation rules to Automation Map.

  A Nunjucks template for JMWE's "Build-your-own (scripted) post-function", run by a
  Scheduled action whose JQL matches ONE anchor work item (e.g. key = OPS-1), daily - so
  the template runs once per run. Contract: docs/push-sync.md.

  Fill the five values below. JMWE has no secret store: the token is readable by anyone
  who can edit JMWE configuration. If the site uses an IP allowlist, add JMWE's egress
  addresses to it (see the JMWE callRest documentation).

  JMWE's Nunjucks has no SHA-256, so the payload is proven by X-Automap-Length (the text's
  length in UTF-16 code units). It cannot escape to ASCII either, so it sends UTF-8 and
  never ends a chunk between the halves of a surrogate pair. Chunks are 80 000 characters:
  at most 240 KB of UTF-8, under the receiver's 256 KiB.

  Each rule is one request; a site with many hundreds of rules may run longer than a
  JMWE action is allowed to. Such a site runs this template as several Scheduled actions,
  each pushing a slice of the rules: PART. Leave it "" on a small site. To split in two,
  make two actions an hour apart with the same values except PART = "1/2" in the first
  and "2/2" in the second; each pushes its half, and the map is built when the last half
  of the day has arrived. Three are "1/3", "2/3", "3/3", up to 20. The limit is honest:
  each copy must finish within JMWE's time limit; raise M until it does. Each rule's part
  is a function of its own id (its uuid's first 8 hex digits modulo M), so a rule made or
  deleted between the actions moves no other rule across the cut; the slices are therefore
  roughly, not exactly, equal. A rule made between the two actions may be missed until
  the next day. The copies find each other by the UTC date they start on, so schedule
  them inside the same UTC day - e.g. 01:00 and 02:00 UTC - never either side of 00:00 UTC.

  Every request is tried up to three times when it gets no answer (a timeout), a 429 or
  a 5xx - at once, since a template cannot wait. A 409 or 422 to the push starts it once
  more under a new run id (a part: the same part again). A 409 to a last chunk sent again
  means the receiver took the first copy and its answer was lost: the push is done.

  This is the first of two templates. automap-usage.njk, a Scheduled action of its own,
  pushes this month's usage and the audit log (beta, Advanced edition), so each gets a
  JMWE action's whole time and a slow audit log never holds up the rules.

  The rendered output is one line saying what happened; it lands in JMWE's logs.

  Copyright MOY Apps. Licensed for use with Automation Map for Jira only; see LICENSE.
-#}
{%- set SITE = "your-site.atlassian.net" -%}
{%- set EMAIL = "you@example.com" -%}
{%- set TOKEN = "an API token with the Automation scope" -%}
{%- set PUSH_URL = "the receiver URL from Automation Map, ending /v1/push" -%}
{%- set KEY = "the amk_ key from Automation Map" -%}
{%- set PART = "" -%}

{%- set NAME = "jmwe" -%}
{%- set VERSION = "1.6.0" -%}
{%- set CHUNK = 80000 -%}
{%- set MAX_PAGES = 100 -%}
{%- set OPTS = { "auth": { "username": EMAIL, "password": TOKEN }, "timeout": 60000 } -%}

{#- callRest with up to three tries: no answer (a timeout gives _error and no _statusCode),
    a 429 or a 5xx is tried again at once. The answer lands in `box` as [answer, tries - 1]:
    a macro renders text, so it hands objects back through an array. `how` is "get" (with
    the token), "post" (a JSON body, with the token) or "push" (text, with `opts` as given) -#}
{%- macro fetch(box, url, how, body, opts) -%}
{%- for tr in range(0, 3) -%}
  {%- if tr < 3 and not box.length -%}
    {%- if how == "push" -%}
      {%- set r = url | callRest(verb="post", body=body, noJSON=true, dontFail=true, options=opts) -%}
    {%- elif how == "post" -%}
      {%- set r = url | callRest(verb="post", body=body, options=OPTS, dontFail=true) -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- set r = url | callRest(options=OPTS, dontFail=true) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if not (r._error or r._statusCode) or (r._statusCode and r._statusCode != 429 and r._statusCode < 500) or tr == 2 -%}
      {%- set _ = box.push(r) -%}
      {%- set _ = box.push(tr) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- PART = "N/M", 1 <= N <= M <= 20, or ""; a bad value stops the action before it reads anything -#}
{%- set pp = (PART | trim).split("/") if PART else [] -%}
{%- set partN = (pp[0] | int) if pp.length == 2 else 0 -%}
{%- set partM = (pp[1] | int) if pp.length == 2 else 0 -%}
{%- set partOk = (not PART) or (pp.length == 2 and ("" + partN) == pp[0] and ("" + partM) == pp[1] and partM >= 2 and partM <= 20 and partN >= 1 and partN <= partM) -%}
{%- set part = (partN + "/" + partM) if (partOk and PART) else "" -%}

{#- parts of one day share the run: the UTC date, worked out from the clock without a date
    library - and stamped now, before the minutes of reading, so copies started on the same
    side of 00:00 UTC agree on it. Without a clock a part cannot name its day -#}
{%- macro ymd(days) -%}
{%- set z = days + 719468 -%}
{%- set era = z // 146097 -%}
{%- set doe = z - era * 146097 -%}
{%- set yoe = (doe - doe // 1460 + doe // 36524 - doe // 146096) // 365 -%}
{%- set doy = doe - (365 * yoe + yoe // 4 - yoe // 100) -%}
{%- set mp = (5 * doy + 2) // 153 -%}
{%- set dd = doy - (153 * mp + 2) // 5 + 1 -%}
{%- set mm = (mp + 3) if mp < 10 else (mp - 9) -%}
{%- set yy = yoe + era * 400 + (1 if mm <= 2 else 0) -%}
{{- yy }}{{ ("0" if mm < 10 else "") + mm }}{{ ("0" if dd < 10 else "") + dd -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- set nowMs = (now | date("x") if now else "0") | int -%}
{%- set dayRun = ("d" + (ymd(nowMs // 86400000) | trim)) if (part and nowMs) else "" -%}
{%- if not partOk -%}
automap-sync {{ NAME }} {{ VERSION }}: failed - [2] PART must be "N/M" with 1 <= N <= M <= 20 (e.g. "1/2"), or "", not "{{ PART }}"
{%- elif part and not nowMs -%}
automap-sync {{ NAME }} {{ VERSION }}: failed - [2] no clock (now): parts need the UTC date
{%- else -%}

{#- 1. the cloud id, then every rule id, page by page. A read the API refuses stops the
    action with "[3]" and what was being read - never a rule's id -#}
{%- set tenant = ("https://" + SITE + "/_edge/tenant_info") | callRest -%}
{%- set API = "https://api.atlassian.com/automation/public/jira/" + tenant.cloudId + "/rest/v1" -%}
{%- set stop = [] -%}
{%- set ids = [] -%}
{%- set pages = [""] -%}
{%- for p in range(0, MAX_PAGES) -%}
  {%- if p < pages.length and not stop.length -%}
    {#- links.next is a query string ("?cursor=...") on Atlassian's API, a full URL elsewhere -#}
    {%- set target = pages[p] if (pages[p] and pages[p].indexOf("http") == 0) else (API + "/rule/summary" + (pages[p] if pages[p] else "?limit=100")) -%}
    {%- set box = [] -%}
    {%- set _ = fetch(box, target, "get") -%}
    {%- set page = box[0] -%}
    {%- if page._statusCode or page._error -%}
      {%- set _ = stop.push("[3] the Automation API answered " + (page._statusCode if page._statusCode else "nothing") + " for the rule list") -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- for item in page.data -%}
        {%- set _ = ids.push(item.uuid if item.uuid else item.id) -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if page.links and page.links.next -%}
        {%- set _ = pages.push(page.links.next) -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{#- the slice: a rule's part is a function of its own id - its first 8 hex digits as a
    number, modulo M, plus 1 - so a rule made or deleted between the actions moves no other
    rule across the cut, whatever order the API listed them in -#}
{%- set total = ids.length -%}
{%- if part -%}
  {%- set _ = ids.sort() -%}
  {%- set mine = [] -%}
  {%- for id in ids -%}
    {%- set v = [0] -%}
    {%- for ci in range(0, 8) -%}
      {%- if ci < 8 -%}
        {%- set d = "0123456789abcdef".indexOf(("" + id).slice(ci, ci + 1) | lower) -%}
        {%- if d >= 0 -%}{%- set _ = v.splice(0, 1, v[0] * 16 + d) -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if v[0] % partM + 1 == partN -%}{%- set _ = mine.push(id) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- set ids = mine -%}
{%- endif -%}

{#- 2. each rule, wrapped in "rule", as compact JSON -#}
{%- set parts = [] -%}
{%- for id in ids -%}
  {%- if not stop.length -%}
    {%- set box = [] -%}
    {%- set _ = fetch(box, API + "/rule/" + id, "get") -%}
    {%- set d = box[0] -%}
    {%- if d._statusCode or d._error -%}
      {%- set _ = stop.push("[3] the Automation API answered " + (d._statusCode if d._statusCode else "nothing") + " for rule " + loop.index + " of " + ids.length) -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- set _ = parts.push({ "rule": (d.rule if d.rule else d) } | dump) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set text = '{"rules":[' + parts.join(",") + '],"sender":{"name":"' + NAME + '","version":"' + VERSION + '","rules":' + parts.length + '}}' -%}

{#- 3. chunk boundaries, never between the two halves of a surrogate pair -#}
{%- set bounds = [0] -%}
{%- for i in range(0, (text.length // CHUNK) + 2) -%}
  {%- set start = bounds[bounds.length - 1] -%}
  {%- if start < text.length -%}
    {%- set end = (start + CHUNK) if (start + CHUNK) < text.length else text.length -%}
    {%- set code = text.charCodeAt(end - 1) -%}
    {%- set end = (end - 1) if (end < text.length and code >= 55296 and code <= 56319) else end -%}
    {%- set _ = bounds.push(end) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{#- 4. push: one run id (a part's is the day's, stamped above), chunks in order, the length
    on the last one. A 409 or 422 starts the push once more: a plain run under a new run id,
    a part under the day's (sent again from chunk 0, it replaces itself). -#}
{%- set failures = [] -%}
{%- set queued = [] -%}
{%- set taken = [] -%}
{%- set again = [] -%}
{%- set count = bounds.length - 1 -%}
{%- for attempt in range(0, 2) -%}
{%- if attempt < 2 and not stop.length and not failures.length and not taken.length and again.length == attempt -%}
{%- set run = dayRun if part else (NAME + "-" + text.length + "-" + ids.length + "-" + nowMs + ("-r" if attempt else "")) -%}
{#- JMWE's range() includes its end (checked live: range(0, 8) reached 8), the standard
    one does not; the guard makes both send exactly `count` chunks -#}
{%- for i in range(0, count) -%}
  {%- if failures.length == 0 and taken.length == 0 and again.length == attempt and i < count -%}
    {#- a map cannot be added to in Nunjucks, so each shape of the headers is written out:
        X-Automap-Part on every chunk of a part, Last and Length on the last chunk -#}
    {%- set headers = {
      "Authorization": "Bearer " + KEY,
      "Content-Type": "text/plain; charset=utf-8",
      "X-Automap-Run": run,
      "X-Automap-Seq": "" + i,
      "X-Automap-Sender": NAME + "/" + VERSION
    } -%}
    {%- if part -%}
      {%- set headers = {
        "Authorization": "Bearer " + KEY,
        "Content-Type": "text/plain; charset=utf-8",
        "X-Automap-Run": run,
        "X-Automap-Seq": "" + i,
        "X-Automap-Sender": NAME + "/" + VERSION,
        "X-Automap-Part": part
      } -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if i == count - 1 and not part -%}
      {%- set headers = {
        "Authorization": "Bearer " + KEY,
        "Content-Type": "text/plain; charset=utf-8",
        "X-Automap-Run": run,
        "X-Automap-Seq": "" + i,
        "X-Automap-Sender": NAME + "/" + VERSION,
        "X-Automap-Last": "1",
        "X-Automap-Length": "" + text.length
      } -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if i == count - 1 and part -%}
      {%- set headers = {
        "Authorization": "Bearer " + KEY,
        "Content-Type": "text/plain; charset=utf-8",
        "X-Automap-Run": run,
        "X-Automap-Seq": "" + i,
        "X-Automap-Sender": NAME + "/" + VERSION,
        "X-Automap-Part": part,
        "X-Automap-Last": "1",
        "X-Automap-Length": "" + text.length
      } -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- set box = [] -%}
    {%- set _ = fetch(box, PUSH_URL, "push", text.slice(bounds[i], bounds[i + 1]), { "headers": headers, "timeout": 60000 }) -%}
    {%- set res = box[0] -%}
    {%- if res._statusCode == 409 and box[1] > 0 and i == count - 1 -%}
      {#- the first copy of the last chunk was taken; its answer was lost on the way back.
          A new run would load the same rules twice; a part sent again would change nothing -#}
      {%- set _ = taken.push(1) -%}
    {%- elif res._statusCode or res._error -%}
      {%- if attempt == 0 and (res._statusCode == 422 or (res._statusCode == 409 and not part)) -%}
        {%- set _ = again.push(1) -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {#- a part's run is the day's: 409 means the map was built today already, or the other
            action has another M; 422 means this part's proof failed twice - run it again -#}
        {%- set _ = failures.push("chunk " + i + ": " + (("HTTP " + res._statusCode) if res._statusCode else "no answer")
            + (" (today's map is already built, or another copy of this action has a different M in PART)" if (part and res._statusCode == 409)
            else (" (this part did not arrive whole; run the action again)" if (part and res._statusCode == 422) else ""))) -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- elif i == count - 1 and ("" + res).indexOf('"queued":true') >= 0 -%}
      {%- set _ = queued.push(1) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
automap-sync {{ NAME }} {{ VERSION }}: {{ ("part " + part + ": " + ids.length + " of " + total + " rules, ") if part else (ids.length + " rules, ") }}{{ text.length }} characters in {{ count }} chunk(s): {{ ("failed - " + stop[0]) if stop.length else (("failed - " + failures.join("; ")) if failures.length else (("part " + part + ": " + ids.length + " rules " + (("already taken (the answer to the last chunk was lost)") if taken.length else ("pushed, " + ("map queued" if queued.length else ("waiting for the other " + ("part" if partM == 2 else "parts")))))) if part else (("the last chunk was already taken; " if taken.length else "") + "pushed, the map is rebuilding"))) }}
{%- endif -%}